  "result": "Excellent! The refactoring is complete and successful. All 311 tests pass.\n\n**Refactoring Summary:**\n\n**New file: src/totals.js**\n- Contains total calculation functions moved from invoices.js:\n  - `lineTotal(line)` - Calculate line item total (qty \u00d7 unitPrice)\n  - `lineDiscount(line)` - Calculate line item discount\n  - `lineVat(line)` - Calculate line item VAT after discount\n  - `invoiceTotals(invoice)` - Calculate all totals: subtotal, discount, VAT, voucher, total\n\n**Updated: src/invoices.js**\n- Imports total functions from totals.js\n- Re-exports them for backward compatibility\n- Removed 50+ lines of calculation code\n- Maintains all existing functionality\n\n**New file: test/totals.test.js**\n- 23 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Basic calculations for each function\n  - Edge cases (zero amounts, full discounts, no VAT, etc.)\n  - Rounding behavior\n  - Multiple lines with different rates\n  - Voucher handling\n  - Complex scenarios with mixed VAT rates and discounts\n\n**Backward Compatibility:**\n\u2713 All functions still importable from `src/invoices.js`\n\u2713 Functions also directly importable from `src/totals.js`\n\u2713 All 288 existing tests still pass\n\u2713 New 23 tests for totals module all pass\n\nThe refactoring successfully separates concerns: invoices.js handles invoice lifecycle, while totals.js handles financial calculations. The codebase is now more modular and maintainable.",
